card.statement:
[<<cite:Bosch:1990fj,EinMus,Ish07>>] Let $X$ be a scheme of finite type over $\C$, $Sch$ the category of schemes of finite type over $\C$, $Set$ the category of sets. The contravariant functor

\begin{align*}
Sch\ra Set,\quad Y\mapsto \Hom_{Sch} (Y\widehat{\times} D,X),
\end{align*}

is represented by a scheme $JX$, that is,

\begin{align*}
\Hom_{Sch}(Y,JX)\cong \Hom_{Sch} (Y\widehat{\times} D,X).
\end{align*}

for any $Y\in Sch$. Here $Y\widehat{\times} D$ is the completion of $Y{\times} D$ with respect to the subscheme $Y\widehat{\times}\{0\}$.
